From 1ff68ab97becdb402be5e9ae3166c50e5a190212 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:55:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(delegation): a terminal unit ends the child rows
 it left open

A backend restart killed async delegation deleg_5facc89f's owner at 10:06:01;
the next process recorded the unit unknown 17 s later, but child session
20261111_094134_4755e7 stayed ended_at NULL for 27 h+: recovery never touched
session rows, and the startup orphan sweep deferred to any live backend whose
heartbeat predated the row (hub backends restart many times a day).

- dispatch persists task_session_ids; recover_abandoned_delegations ends the
  unit's still-open subagent rows of that parent (delegation_unknown), and a
  stall force-finalize does the same (delegation_stalled).
- SessionDB.end_subagents_of_ended_parents: the startup sweep ends an idle
  subagent row whose parent row has ended, with no heartbeat guess
  (parent_ended_reap). Distinct reasons, so the reap's killed-subagent notice
  is not re-sent to a chat that already got the delegation's result.
